from ./Cli import Cli
from ./Config import Config
from ./Fonts import Fonts
from ./HtmlOutput import HtmlOutput
from ./OutputSize import OutputSize
from ./PngOutput import PngOutput
from ./SvgOutput import SvgOutput

export anchor Output:
    description:
        The compiler output targets and how they map.

    summary:
        Every rendered composition can be written as HTML, SVG and PNG. The
        three are the same design in three formats, and should look the same.

    fidelity:
        The outputs are expected to match:

        - svg
            Emul computes the layout, shapes the text and draws every box
            itself. The SVG is the reference rendering.
        - png
            The PNG is the SVG rasterized. It adds nothing and leaves nothing
            out, so it always matches the SVG.
        - html
            The browser does the layout and drawing, from CSS that Emul
            writes. Emul's properties are deliberately a small, plain subset
            of CSS, so a browser and Emul's own layout give nearly the same
            result.

        The HTML and SVG are expected to match closely, not to the pixel.
        Differences in anti-aliasing, glyph smoothing and pixel snapping are
        how each browser draws, and are fine. A difference a person would
        notice, such as a box in clearly the wrong place or a line of text
        breaking at a different word, is a bug in Emul. Emul's designs are
        plain enough that this level of agreement holds in practice.

    sharedInputs:
        All three outputs are made from the same inputs, so they never drift
        apart. They share the following.

        - the same output size, as described in @{OutputSize}
        - the same font files, as described in @{Fonts}
        - the same images, read from the same local files

    canvas:
        The output size sets the canvas, which is the area the composition's
        root fills. The root's children are laid out inside it, and
        percentages on them are measured against it. Anything drawn outside
        the canvas is clipped, in all three outputs.

        Behind the root is the canvas background. It is transparent unless a
        background colour is set in @{Config} or on the command line.

    formats:
        - @{HtmlOutput}
        - @{SvgOutput}
        - @{PngOutput}

    choosing:
        Which formats are written is set by the formats setting in @{Config},
        and can be overridden on the command line, as described in @{Cli}.
